    "channel": "Owner decision on the Gate G9 Closure Report (download/Rent_Control_System_Gate_G9_Closure_Report.docx)",
    "minute": {
      "reference": "CM-P8-G9-01",
      "status": "SIGNED",
      "g9Ref": "GATE-G9-2026-09-11",
      "signedBy": "Owner",
      "signedAt": "2026-09-10T17:05:22.013Z",
      "lessons": [
        "Migration succeeded because the register was treated as the contract: Dir. Art. 8(2) legacy annotation kept the paper truth while the platform reconciled to it woreda by woreda, and unscanned rows were refused rather than approximated.",
        "Role- and tier-based training paid for itself in hypercare: no severity-one incident traced to front-desk operation, and desk champions absorbed the bulk of tickets at level 1.",
        "Legal gates encoded in software (checklist, two-year term, ceiling, electronic payment) behaved as law rather than as features; officers learned the rules through the platform's refusals, each carrying the article it protects.",
        "Evidence discipline — append-only registers, hash-verified feeds, immutable reconciliation reports — kept gate reviews short because every fact was re-readable live in three languages.",
        "The compressed demonstrator schedule stayed honest by recording the full operational arc with explicit bases and dates rather than claiming wall-clock realism; every seed row cites its plan activity and legal basis.",
        "Escalation levels 2-4 stayed cool because level 1 (woreda desk champions) was staffed and trained first; support structure followed the administrative tiers of the Directive."
      ],
      "transitions": [
        "Wave 2 (city-wide, remaining 10 sub-cities): checklist green and sequencing gates satisfied; the cutover order rests with city operations under runbook v1.1 wave procedure.",
        "Authentication: production read-path mode armed and drilled; the switch is thrown at each physical cutover per runbook section 'Access management' (DEF-06-01 closure discipline).",
        "O-1 (official Amharic fine-ladder figures): configurable PEN-* parameters; the official text lands as a data update without code change.",
        "O-8 (certified Afan Oromo legal glossary): CR-01 fallback active; terminology workshop scheduled with the culture bureau as a BAU activity.",
        "Improvement backlog BL-01..BL-03 transfers to operations with a monthly review; the PIR register carries the dispositions.",
        "Ministry feed continues monthly under runbook v1.1; periods are immutable and hash-verified."
      ],
      "openItems": [
        "O-1: CLOSED_BY_DISPOSITION — configurable penalty parameters await the official figures; engine reads parameters, never constants.",
        "O-8: HANDOVER — certified glossary workshop with the culture bureau; trilingual fallback active (CR-01/NFR-06).",
        "DEF-08-01: CLOSED — hosting FD provisioning documented in operations manual v1.1.",
        "Defect register: no open defects at any severity at closure (DEF-06-01..03, DEF-07-01..02, DEF-08-01..02 all closed)."
      ]
    }
  },
